HARK! "A Most Ingenious Paradox"
  or, "In Which the Fibonacci Sequence is Computed and Found Perfectly Satisfactory"

(ASIDE, AT SOME LENGTH:
  Young Frederic, being a slave of duty, has undertaken to compute
  the Fibonacci sequence up to a given term. His mathematical indentures
  are quite clear on the matter: each number is the sum of the two
  preceding numbers, by which circumstance he finds himself quite unable
  to deviate from the formula, however inconvenient it may prove.

  "A paradox, a paradox, a most ingenious paradox!"
  — The Pirates of Penzance
END OF ASIDE.)

PRINCIPALS
  PRAY WELCOME n     AS A PEER  ASIDE: which term to compute up to
  PRAY WELCOME a     AS A PEER  BEING 0
  PRAY WELCOME b     AS A PEER  BEING 1
  PRAY WELCOME temp  AS A PEER  BEING 0
  PRAY WELCOME i     AS A PEER  BEING 0

ASIDE: -----------------------------------------------------------------------
ASIDE: DUTY THE FIRST: a recursive function to compute the nth Fibonacci term
ASIDE: -----------------------------------------------------------------------

IT IS MY DUTY TO PERFORM fibonacci UNDER THE TERMS OF n
  ASIDE: base cases — as Frederic's piratical indentures clearly specify
  ALIKE n AND 0
  SHOULD IT TRANSPIRE THAT
    QUITE SO.
      AND SO I FIND 0
  SO MUCH FOR THAT.

  ALIKE n AND 1
  SHOULD IT TRANSPIRE THAT
    QUITE SO.
      AND SO I FIND 1
  SO MUCH FOR THAT.

  ASIDE: the recursive case — duty demands we proceed
  AND SO I FIND ~
    SUM OF ~
      SUMMON fibonacci WITH DIFFERENCE OF n AND 1 IF YOU PLEASE. ~
      AND SUMMON fibonacci WITH DIFFERENCE OF n AND 2 IF YOU PLEASE.
MY DUTY IS DISCHARGED.

ASIDE: -----------------------------------------------------------------------
ASIDE: DUTY THE SECOND: solicit the term from the audience
ASIDE: -----------------------------------------------------------------------

BEHOLD "A MOST INGENIOUS PARADOX"
BEHOLD "Please state the number of terms you require:"
PRAY TELL n
n IS HENCEFORTH A PEER

BEHOLD WOVEN OF "The first " AND n AND " terms of the Fibonacci sequence:" IF YOU PLEASE.
BEHOLD "--------------------------------------------"

ASIDE: -----------------------------------------------------------------------
ASIDE: DUTY THE THIRD: print the sequence iteratively (more efficient for display)
ASIDE: -----------------------------------------------------------------------

a IS APPOINTED 0
b IS APPOINTED 1
i IS APPOINTED 0

BY A LEGAL FICTION KNOWN AS sequence WHILST UNLIKE i AND LARGER OF i AND DIFFERENCE OF n AND 1

  ASIDE: output the current term with appropriate ceremony
  BEHOLD WOVEN OF "  Term " AND SUM OF i AND 1 AND ": " AND a IF YOU PLEASE.

  ASIDE: advance the sequence — indentures demand it
  temp IS APPOINTED b
  b IS APPOINTED SUM OF a AND b
  a IS APPOINTED temp

  i IS APPOINTED SUM OF i AND 1

THE TERM EXPIRES.

BEHOLD "--------------------------------------------"
BEHOLD WOVEN OF "The " AND n AND "th term (recursive confirmation): " ~
  AND SUMMON fibonacci WITH DIFFERENCE OF n AND 1 IF YOU PLEASE. ~
  IF YOU PLEASE.
BEHOLD "The computation is complete. Frederic's duty is discharged."

FINALE.
